+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry validates a call against the registered tool's JSON Schema before an executor can observe it.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` checks an input against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor; rejected input returns a `ToolResponse` describing the invalid field and does not invoke the executor ([validated by: rejects invalid input without exposing values and preserves valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L18)).
+- Valid input, including undeclared extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once ([validated by: rejects invalid input without exposing values and preserves valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L18)).
+- An invalid schema fails during static tool registration with an error naming the tool ([validated by: rejects an invalid schema when registering its tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L61)).
+- A static schema is compiled at registration and reused across repeated executions ([validated by: compiles a static schema at registration and reuses it for ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L73)).
+- A function-valued definition is resolved for each execution, and its current schema governs that call ([validated by: validates function sourced tools against the current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L106)).
+- A rejected tool call is returned to the provider as a tool result so a later round can correct the input ([validated by: returns a rejected call to the provider so it can correct the input next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L134)).
